# Git blame — ignore these commits when computing line-level blame.
# Bulk format / rename passes belong here: including them hides the actual
# author of every line they touched.
#
# Format: one 40-char (or abbreviated) SHA per line, with the commit
# subject as a comment above it. Configure git once with:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Deliberately empty. The four SHAs listed here previously belonged to the
# private repo's history; this repo starts from a single commit, so those
# revs do not exist. Note that `git blame --ignore-revs-file` FAILS on an
# unknown rev rather than skipping it, so a stale SHA here breaks blame
# for everyone who has the config set.
